Now I understand the full picture. The core report logic is well-tested, but there are two real gaps that the task and my day-124 lesson point at:

1. **The /status verdict path is not testable end-to-end.** reflex_effectiveness_summary() hardcodes the real path; there's no path-parameterized helper the /status wiring shares. So the actual verdict-word-from-file path (the thing /status calls) is never exercised with synthetic data — the day-124 "conditionally-asserting/silently-skipping" risk lives exactly here.

